WEBVTT

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:08.890
I've had three tours of duty overseas
both in Iraq and Afghanistan,

00:00:09.128 --> 00:00:16.090
and one horrible day where
my platoon was traveling.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.010
My Humvee got hit by an IED.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:26.760
Two people died that day,
and I was severely injured.

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.780
I broke three bones.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.660
I had burns all over my body.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:33.560
I had a traumatic brain injury.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:39.249
When I was back in the rehabilitation
center in the U.S.,

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:42.480
one of my symptoms was tinnitus.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.200
I had a lot of healing to do.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.432
Being told that the tinnitus was
something that I might have to deal

00:00:51.472 --> 00:00:56.340
with my entire life was a very
difficult thing to internalize.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.790
But after talking
to an audiologist and realizing

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:05.900
things that I could do
to make it better, it helped.

00:01:06.660 --> 00:01:10.328
Before then, I was mostly
going out drinking,

00:01:10.368 --> 00:01:15.880
trying to deal with it in the most
unhealthy way as possible.

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:23.920
But after being told that I can enrich
my environment with sound, so the tinnitus

00:01:25.854 --> 00:01:33.354
isn't as noticeable, now I've started
playing nice sounds, music, ocean noises,

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:39.820
frogs, birds chirping.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:44.117
It actually all helps,
and I find that I don't deal

00:01:44.157 --> 00:01:48.020
with my tinnitus in quite
as unhealthy ways anymore.

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:52.545
So, just being able to deal with that one

00:01:52.585 --> 00:01:58.340
symptom makes my healing
process so much better.
